src/meshtastic.c and include/tsim/meshtastic.h (candidate 1) are adapted from Meshtasticator,
https://github.com/meshtastic/Meshtasticator, by its contributors, licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
The MAC and routing timing follow its lib/mac.py and lib/node.py; the code is a rewrite in C, and
the differences from Meshtasticator are listed in include/tsim/meshtastic.h.

The maps and results in scenarios/meshtasticator/ are output of Meshtasticator, recorded by
tools/meshtasticator.py, which names the Meshtasticator commit that produced them.

src/meshcore.c and include/tsim/meshcore.h (candidate 2) are adapted from MeshCore,
https://github.com/meshcore-dev/MeshCore, Copyright (c) 2025 Scott Powell / rippleradios.com,
licensed under the MIT License (reproduced below). The routing and dispatcher timing follow
src/Dispatcher.cpp, src/Mesh.cpp, src/helpers/BaseChatMesh.cpp and the simple_repeater and
companion_radio examples at the tags repeater-v1.17.1 and companion-v1.17.1; the code is a rewrite
in C, and the differences from MeshCore are listed in include/tsim/meshcore.h.

The link losses and results in scenarios/meshbench/ are output of MeshBench,
https://github.com/MeshBench/meshbench, recorded by tools/meshbench.py from its Fife network, whose
node positions MeshBench took from CoreScope. They are numbers by node index; no names or positions
are kept.

